cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these findings or certificates, please cite this repository."
title: "The 3x3 matrix multiplication tensor: verified findings around rank 23"
authors:
  - name: "RakTikoo"
version: 1.4.0
date-released: 2026-11-24
license: MIT
keywords:
  - matrix multiplication
  - tensor rank
  - Brent equations
  - Laderman
  - computational algebra
abstract: "Exact Jacobian kernel dimensions at Laderman's and Perminov's rank-23 schemes for the 3x3 matrix multiplication tensor (kernel 76 and 94 over Q; excess over trivial tangents 6 and 24), a covering-parity case split for term-repair instances, five completely decided repair instances, a flip-component census of Perminov's cn122, exact pair-merge exclusions, and a completely decided quarters exclusion (174/174 cases UNSAT) — all with machine-checkable certificates. Version 1.1.0 adds a census showing every unit term in the banked rank-23 schemes is a naive term (41 of 41), kernel measurements at Perminov's cr58_cn122 and at ranks 24 and 26 showing no monotone behaviour in the rank, a bounded cross-family transplant census, and an exact audit of two claims in a January 2026 report. Version 1.2.0 adds an extension of the unit-term census to every other verified scheme on the campaign disk (49 of 50 unit terms naive, with a single rank-24 counterexample, so the universal form does not extend beyond the original bank) and a cluster anatomy of the three rank-23 schemes under one fixed greedy procedure. Version 1.3.0 adds a census of the complete Heule–Kauers–Seidl repository of rank-23 schemes (17,376 schemes, all with entries in {−1, 0, 1}; all 1,882 unit terms naive, no off-support unit term in the population), an anatomy of the campaign's homotopy walks showing their terms-merging trips were anti-parallel cancellation artefacts of an unsigned monitor, the closure of the cross-scheme transplant census at all cardinalities ≤ 4 across the 60-scheme enlarged bank (the only hits are the constructed split's own undoing), and a single-drop delta table over six schemes spanning ranks 23–26 (a wrong=1 neighbour exactly where a unit term exists; the one off-support flavour at proj-24). Version 1.4.0 adds the decided free-4 repair fronts (1,843/1,843 and 336/336 cases UNSAT) and three partial fronts with their decided fractions and a lost run disclosed, the closure of the walk line, the exact ruler geometry at Perminov's cn122 (21 lines, no rank drop, no merges even over the complex numbers at the tested scope) and the unique grip-gain scheme gg611 on those lines, a calibrated 3-adic Hensel bridge from F3 to Q (the method is published prior art; the calibration and one native-point conversion are ours), a one-signedness census of 11,777 near-miss states (all residuals +E_e; unit terms 2,010 positive against 1 negative), exact exclusions of the Gamma39 Singer ansatz over F3 and of involution pairing, a feasibility verdict on the C13-only Singer ansatz (solver run in flight, undecided), the lensC rank-26 shear/drop pipeline (10,495 wrong=1 states; repairs would be rank 25, not 22), the border line's conversion equivalence and calibration anatomy, a case study closing the neighbourhood of the closest F3 near-miss our searches have produced (a 22-term state with 5 wrong entries of 729), a census of symmetry groups over F3 (three survivor specifications; D13 and Q12 not realisable), a validated substitution-method instrument whose certified bounds sit below the published ones, a learned near-partition pattern in support shapes (validated as a signature; its ten best proposals all provably empty), and a GPU evaluator benchmark. It also records that over F2 the rank is now determined to be exactly 23 by others' 2026 work (Tomar, arXiv:2610.11823, and the chain it completes), so rank 22 over F2 is excluded; over Q and F3 rank 22 remains open. No rank-22 decomposition is claimed."
